From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 117/159] wifi: ath10k: Skip hwmon temperature on WCN3990

The WCN3990 firmware advertises WMI_SERVICE_THERM_THROT, so
ath10k_thermal_register() registers both the cooling device and an
hwmon temperature sensor, but the firmware never answers
WMI_TLV_PDEV_GET_TEMPERATURE_CMDID. Every read of temp1_input sends the
command, waits ATH10K_THERMAL_SYNC_TIMEOUT_HZ (5 s) for an event that
never comes, logs "failed to synchronize thermal read" and returns
-ETIMEDOUT.

Tools such as lm-sensors read every hwmon device, so each run stalls
for 5 seconds and reports N/A. The read also holds conf_mutex for the
whole timeout, blocking configuration changes on the interface.

Seen on SM7250 (Motorola Moto G 5G Plus) with firmware
WLAN.HL.3.3.1-00694-QCAHLSWMTPLZ-1.

Add a no_temperature_read hardware parameter, set it for WCN3990 and
do not register the hwmon device when it is set. The cooling device
for thermal throttling is still registered.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c    | 1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h      | 5 +++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
index 7c2939cbde5f..548efe4f530c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -746,6 +746,7 @@ static const struct ath10k_hw_params ath10k_hw_params_list[] = {
 		.use_fw_tx_credits = false,
 		.delay_unmap_buffer = true,
 		.mcast_frame_registration = false,
+		.no_temperature_read = true,
 	},
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
index cd468b24bd33..c18fae981270 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
@@ -638,6 +638,11 @@ struct ath10k_hw_params {
 
 	/* The hardware support multicast frame registrations */
 	bool mcast_frame_registration;
+
+	/* The firmware advertises thermal throttling but never answers a
+	 * temperature request
+	 */
+	bool no_temperature_read;
 };
 
 struct htt_resp;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
index 9bb486f8e920..c08a1d9ae57a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
@@ -183,7 +183,8 @@ int ath10k_thermal_register(struct ath10k *ar)
 	/* Do not register hwmon device when temperature reading is not
 	 * supported by firmware
 	 */
-	if (!(ar->wmi.ops->gen_pdev_get_temperature))
+	if (!(ar->wmi.ops->gen_pdev_get_temperature) ||
+	    ar->hw_params.no_temperature_read)
 		return 0;
 
 	/* Avoid linking error on devm_hwmon_device_register_with_groups, I
